      <scopecontent id="aspace_e569c2c85016173a41fbaa865348c470">
         <head>Scope and Contents</head>
         <p>This collection contains administrative files including rights and reproduction requests, transparencies, and photographs of artwork belonging to the Yale Center for British Art.</p>
      </scopecontent>
      <bioghist id="aspace_4d56c6891dff522fcae3420cbdf486a1">
         <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
         <p>The Imaging Services department is responsible for the creation, digitization, and management of new and existing photography of the museum's collections, architecture, and selected events. Originally a part of the Office of the Registrar before becoming an independent department in 2012, Imaging Services works to document the museum's collections, and to maintain image and rights-related information in both the museum's collections management database and the digital asset management system. The department also handles technical photography for the museum's Conservation department, including infrared and ultraviolet digital imaging. Imaging Services staff members serve as a resource for the museum and the university in the areas of digital photography, fine art reproduction, copyright, and digital asset management.</p>
      </bioghist>
      <accessrestrict id="aspace_180953489d09de1db92ad7e58142973c">
         <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
         <p>This collection is unprocessed and may not be available for immediate access.</p>
      </accessrestrict>
